~ start
President Larrañaga: Forgive the heat, Mr President. In Spain we hold our summits in courtyards because it is the only room with a roof that breathes.
- Raise the Pyrenees power link => pyrenees
- Raise the drought and water => water
- Raise tourism and housing => tourism
~ pyrenees
President Larrañaga: The link under the mountains. We could light half of Europe with our sun if only the cable existed.
- Commit to the cable => cable
- Ask for guarantees on prices => prices
~ cable
President Larrañaga: A cable, then. It will cost more than promised, and arrive late, and be wonderful.
=> END
~ prices
President Larrañaga: Guarantees on prices. You want the sun to stay cheap. So do we, naturally.
=> END
~ water
President Larrañaga: The rivers are thinner each year, and the farmers' unions louder. Neither of those is a coincidence.
- Offer French desalination expertise => desal
- Offer a joint water charter => charter
~ desal
President Larrañaga: Desalination, yes. The coast will take it, the interior will ask what about us.
=> END
~ charter
President Larrañaga: A charter. A very European answer, with a preamble longer than the river.
=> END
~ tourism
President Larrañaga: Fourteen million of yours come every year and half of them break something. I say this with great affection.
- Propose a joint housing programme => housing
- Propose a tourist levy => levy
~ housing
President Larrañaga: Housing is the quiet crisis. A joint programme would give my mayors something to point at other than the beach.
=> END
~ levy
President Larrañaga: A levy, applied to your people and mine alike. The hotels will protest, and the cities will frame the first bill.
=> END
